{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Do not require online platforms to promote selected media organisations",
        "additional_details": "Many commercial platforms succeed because they recommend content based on each person\u2019s interests. Whether someone watches educational videos, gaming, history, science or independent journalism, recommendations should reflect those choices. Public Service Media should compete by creating content people choose to watch, not through regulatory preference. In our view, government should not influence what content platforms recommend to viewers.",
        "background": "We urge the Government to abandon proposals in the \u201cWatch This Space\u201d consultation that would require online platforms to promote selected media organisations through recommendation systems, and protect viewer choice by keeping recommendations based on users\u2019 interests.",
